.TH TEST-ALL 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "Developer Commands"
.SH NAME
test-all \- run Kagi's standard local validation suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/test-all
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks Rust formatting, compiles all targets, runs the test suite, and runs
Clippy.
On Linux it also checks the eBPF userspace loader and the optional ISA-L,
IPP, and AOCL build paths.
.PP
The script checks CUDA, HIP, and OpenCL when it detects their development
toolchains.
A check on a host without a supported device can exercise CPU fallback.
Use the repository's hardware validation workflow to establish execution on
the device.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STRICT
Set to 1 to deny warnings in the default Clippy pass.
The feature-specific Clippy passes always deny warnings.
.TP
.B ROCM_PATH
ROCm installation directory used to find
.BR hipcc .
The default is
.IR /opt/rocm .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coverage (1),
.BR kagi-build (1),
.BR kagi-security-check (1)
